WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.016
Cedric's mother was busy writing a letter when her servant interrupted.

2
00:00:05.017 --> 00:00:11.237
"You have a visitor." The maid's eyes were wide with excitement.

3
00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:16.970
"It's the Earl of Dorincourt!"

4
00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:20.972
Mrs. Errol entered the main room of the cottage.

5
00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:25.127
A fierce-looking man was standing by the fireplace.

6
00:00:25.128 --> 00:00:33.649
"Mrs. Errol . . ." The earl paused to look into her eyes, which reminded him of Cedric's.

7
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.488
"Your son looks so much like you."

8
00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:45.156
"People often say that," she said. "But I like to think he also resembles his father."

9
00:00:45.157 --> 00:00:54.302
"Yes," the earl hesitantly agreed. "He . . . he is like my son too."

10
00:00:54.303 --> 00:01:02.193
Mrs. Errol took a seat on one side of the fireplace. "Please sit down, my lord."

11
00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:05.272
The earl was too agitated to sit.

12
00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:10.684
But he was impressed that she didn't seem troubled by his sudden arrival.

13
00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:14.936
"Do you know why I'm here?" he asked.

14
00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:17.734
"Mr. Havisham has told me that a woman—"

15
00:01:17.735 --> 00:01:24.533
"I've come to say that her claims will be investigated and challenged," the earl jumped in.

16
00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:28.225
"Your son's rights will be protected."

17
00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:35.616
"Cedric must have nothing that's not legally his," Mrs. Errol said in a soft voice.

18
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:43.294
The earl waved his hand dismissively. "That outrageous woman and her child—"

19
00:01:43.295 --> 00:01:50.241
Mrs. Errol shrugged. "Perhaps she cares for her son as much as I care for Cedric, my lord."

20
00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:53.848
Mrs. Errol was respectful but firm.

21
00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:57.797
The earl noticed again that she was not intimidated.

22
00:01:57.798 --> 00:02:03.071
It reminded him of how unafraid Cedric had been when they first met.

23
00:02:03.072 --> 00:02:05.219
Mrs. Errol went on.

24
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:10.526
"If this woman is your older son's wife, then her son is Lord Fauntleroy.

25
00:02:10.527 --> 00:02:12.758
And mine is not."

26
00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:20.986
The earl frowned. "I suppose you'd prefer that Cedric not be the Earl of Dorincourt."

27
00:02:20.987 --> 00:02:25.865
Mrs. Errol's face turned red, and she looked away for a moment.

28
00:02:25.866 --> 00:02:29.724
"It's a wonderful thing to be the Earl of Dorincourt.

29
00:02:29.725 --> 00:02:36.947
But it's more important that Cedric be like his father—brave, honest, and kind."

30
00:02:36.948 --> 00:02:45.966
The earl smiled slightly. "In contrast to what I have been, eh?"

31
00:02:45.967 --> 00:02:50.951
"I haven't had the pleasure of knowing you, but I know that my son believes—"

32
00:02:50.952 --> 00:02:59.409
Mrs. Errol looked directly at the earl. "I know that Cedric loves you."

33
00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:05.601
"Would he love me if you'd revealed why I never allowed you to visit the castle?"

34
00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:10.349
"No, and that's exactly why I never told him."

35
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:14.846
The earl was momentarily stunned by her reply.

36
00:03:14.847 --> 00:03:20.636
"Well . . . well, most people would have told him."

37
00:03:20.637 --> 00:03:28.188
He started to pace the room again. "When Cedric arrived, I was tired of my life.

38
00:03:28.189 --> 00:03:31.427
But he has given me something to live for.

39
00:03:31.428 --> 00:03:36.690
I'd be proud for him to succeed me as head of the family."

40
00:03:36.691 --> 00:03:44.307
The earl stopped right in front of Mrs. Errol. On the verge of tears, he said, "I am miserable!

41
00:03:44.308 --> 00:03:48.973
And it's because I'm miserable that I've come to you."

42
00:03:48.974 --> 00:03:55.138
Mrs. Errol noted that his hands were shaking and his voice was unsteady.

43
00:03:55.139 --> 00:03:58.067
She waited for him to go on.

44
00:03:58.068 --> 00:04:03.655
"I used to hate you, and I was jealous of you."

45
00:04:03.656 --> 00:04:09.566
Some of the earl's usual authority returned before he started to break down again.

46
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:13.492
"This terrible business has changed all that.

47
00:04:13.493 --> 00:04:18.531
I'm here because Cedric loves you, and I love him.

48
00:04:18.532 --> 00:04:24.650
I've treated you badly, so I don't deserve any kindness from you.

49
00:04:24.651 --> 00:04:30.281
But treat me as well as you can, for Cedric's sake."

50
00:04:30.282 --> 00:04:34.685
Mrs. Errol was touched by his remarks.

51
00:04:34.686 --> 00:04:38.692
She stood up and moved the other chair closer to the earl.

52
00:04:38.693 --> 00:04:41.106
"I wish you would sit."

53
00:04:41.107 --> 00:04:45.348
She placed a reassuring hand on the earl's arm.

54
00:04:45.349 --> 00:04:49.086
"You're upset, and you need all your strength."

55
00:04:49.087 --> 00:04:54.931
The earl allowed her to help him sit, but he wiggled uncomfortably in the chair.

56
00:04:54.932 --> 00:04:59.350
"May I place a pillow behind your back?" Mrs. Errol asked.

57
00:04:59.351 --> 00:05:03.506
"That might make you feel better."

58
00:05:03.507 --> 00:05:08.096
She took a small pillow from the sofa and slipped it into place.

59
00:05:08.097 --> 00:05:11.586
The earl gave a nod and a quick smile.

60
00:05:11.587 --> 00:05:16.909
He was strangely comforted by this woman with the soothing voice and manner.

61
00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:22.671
Mrs. Errol was a good listener, which led him to talk even more about Cedric.

62
00:05:22.672 --> 00:05:26.110
Soon the earl was feeling much better.

63
00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:31.801
"This is a cheerful room. Do you like this house?" he asked.

64
00:05:31.802 --> 00:05:35.096
"Very much," Mrs. Errol said.

65
00:05:35.097 --> 00:05:39.643
"I couldn't ask for a lovelier house and garden."

66
00:05:39.644 --> 00:05:45.804
"And you, Mrs. Errol, are a lovely person," the earl thought.

67
00:05:45.805 --> 00:05:49.589
"Cedric is lucky that you're his mother."

68
00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:53.193
He wasn't ready to say those words aloud.

69
00:05:53.194 --> 00:05:59.759
Instead he said, "May I come again to talk over this matter?"

70
00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:06.859
"You're welcome here as often as you like, my lord." Mrs. Errol smiled brightly.

71
00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:13.437
"I'm always happy to talk about Cedric!"

